{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>On the third day, the prince, etc.</b> On the third day the prince offering was Zevulun — and so for all of them. But for Netanel, concerning whom it says הִקְרִיב נְתַנְאֵל, the expression that follows is to say 'the prince of Yissaskhar' — because his name and his offering have already been mentioned. And for the others, in whom הִקְרִיב is not said, this expression falls upon them — 'the prince of the children of such-and-such' — that day the prince offering was for the tribe of such-and-such."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:52.072216264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}